# Agent modes (CHAT vs EQA_EPISODE)

One skill library (`emet.agent.skills`); **two orchestrators**. Do not merge them or expect Discord chat to score Habitat MCQ.

| Mode | Entry | Pack builder | Stop |
|------|-------|--------------|------|
| **CHAT** | `emet run agent` (Discord / terminal) | `get_tools` → `build_skill_pack(CHAT)` | User turns |
| **EQA_EPISODE** | Habitat / dynagraph when `eqa.agentic_verify` | `build_agentic_eqa_tools` → `build_skill_pack(EQA_EPISODE)` | Verify-gated `submit_answer` / explore `finish` |

## Shared contract

- JSON `{"tool_calls":[...],"message":...}` + `parse_tool_calls_response`
- Conceptual aliases (different **names** — do **not** rename EQA tools; traces depend on them):
  - scan: CHAT `scan_environment` ↔ EQA `look_around`
  - explore: CHAT `explore` ↔ EQA `explore_frontier`

## Keep packs disjoint

- **CHAT-only**: `describe_scene`, Discord `send_*`, emotes, `rotate_base`, `quit`, … (`CHAT_EXCLUSIVE_TOOL_NAMES`)
- **EQA-only**: `investigate` / `navigate_to_obs`, `verify_siglip`, `submit_answer` / `finish`, `inspect_graph` (`EQA_EXCLUSIVE_TOOL_NAMES`)
- Membership tests: `src/test/agent/test_skill_packs.py`

## Common confusions

- **`--eqa` on chat** = caption/VLM for `describe_scene` — **not** the Habitat agentic episode loop
- **`--eqa-eval`** = Habitat harness path; bypasses the chat tool-router
- Chat “are you sure?” / “look at X” ≈ `face_toward` + `describe_scene` (not blind ±45°); EQA would `navigate_to_obs` + `verify_siglip`

Docs: [AGENT_RUN.md](../../docs/AGENT_RUN.md#skill-library-vs-orchestrator-modes), [evaluation.md](../../docs/evaluation.md#agentic-grapheqa-verify--offline-tuning).

## Giant files (do not ingest whole)

Callers outside this package import `GraphEQAMemory` / `AgenticEQAExecutor` / `run_agentic_eqa` from [`emet.memory.graph_eqa`](../../src/emet/memory/graph_eqa/__init__.py), not from mixin modules.

[`agentic_eqa.py`](../../src/emet/memory/graph_eqa/agentic_eqa.py) is a thin facade (~200 lines). Behavior lives in `agentic_{init,run,router,answer,verify,assess,capture,investigate,place,explore,action}.py`. [`graph_memory.py`](../../src/emet/memory/graph_eqa/graph_memory.py) is a thin facade (~200 lines). Types live in `graph_types.py`; `GraphEQAMemory` methods live in `graph_{init,mutate,rooms,eqa_obs,hypotheses,prompt,nav,answer}.py`. Loading a 7k-line module in full (or in many parallel chunks) crashes the Cursor agent host (Mode B / V8 `invalid opcode`). Edit the sibling that owns the method, not the facade. Do not dump agent transcripts or previous crash UIs into the next prompt.
